# Line endings, settled once.
#
# core.autocrlf is on at system level (GitHub Desktop sets it), so git has been
# converting LF to CRLF on checkout. Every file in the repository is stored as
# LF — `git ls-files --eol` says i/lf for all of them — but the working tree
# drifted: engine/model.py sat at w/crlf and builder/index.html at w/mixed.
#
# That drift is not cosmetic. Twice in one day it turned a two-line fix into a
# file git reported as wholly rewritten, and once it hid a real corruption
# inside the noise. Pinning the working tree to LF makes what is on disk, what
# is in a commit, and what GitHub Desktop shows in a diff the same thing.
#
# Nothing is rewritten by adding this: the stored content is already LF, so the
# next checkout simply stops converting it. No `git add --renormalize` needed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf   binary
